  "review": {
    "review": "Root read complete eight-file native/C/raw/safe/test diff, README, build commands, documentation and independent policy review. Exact live bases and staged sources verified.",
    "independent_review": "/private/tmp/eredu-observable-retirement-pass-review.md",
    "independent_review_sha256": "5a7e5f021c74c8f7a76a3067cec1151c1e108a7276cc88aae864d51381b5ac45",
    "behavior": [
      "The new native pass factors the existing full entry-time scan; old void callers delegate unchanged. Only positively settled current-thread records detach.",
      "Busy exits before registry mutation; runtime contention exits before the C call. No progress/evaluation/wait/housekeeping is introduced.",
      "Detached records destroy outside the registry lock under ordinary native runtime serialization; Rust allocation owners remain separately queued for unlocked reclamation.",
      "The C shim preserves original native errors and leaves output untouched on failure. Raw values and safe scalar representation agree; unknown values reject.",
      "Four safe tests and three scenarios in an isolated C++ executable exercise actual lock contention, no hidden progress, full129 scan, correct owner threads, unlocked destruction and actual backing alias lifetime. Existing fairness executable stays unchanged."
    ],
    "limits": [
      "CompleteSnapshot is traversal only, with no completion, caller-root release, allocation-credit or perchunk-peak guarantee.",
      "Record/resource destruction can take unbounded host time. Metadata initialization/errors may allocate.",
      "New code remains within existing safemlx/safemlx-sys unsafe boundary; no portable/native-backend unsafe exception.",
      "Canonical chunk association, carrier cleanup and original admission integration remain separate unfinished work."
    ]
  },
  "behavior": [
    "The existing full entry-time scan returns CompleteSnapshot or Busy; old ordinary callers preserve their behavior.",
    "Only already settled records on their exact original owner thread detach, under the registry mutex, and destroy outside that mutex.",
    "Runtime and registry contention report Busy without hidden housekeeping, progress, polling, waiting, evaluation or tensor allocation.",
    "C/raw/safe bindings preserve native errors; unknown raw results reject. Rust allocation owners remain queued until explicit unlocked reclamation.",
    "Fresh full CPU and content-addressed Metal builds execute both isolated native regressions. No generated source or single-object override is used."
  ],
  "corrections": [],
  "limits": [
    "CompleteSnapshot is not completion evidence, a byte-credit measurement, a registry-empty claim or permission to discard caller roots.",
    "Eligible resource destructors can block; registry/error initialization and exception formatting can allocate host metadata.",
    "The new isolated executable has three scenarios counted as one execution per build; native regression scenarios submit no tensor work.",
    "Canonical chunk association, failure-safe carrier retention/release and next-chunk physical-budget enforcement remain unfinished.",
    "No new released-checkpoint measurement or native distributed validation is included; managed gates remain unchanged."
  ]
